      "reason": "Both quotes state that the Eiffel Tower was closed/did not open. The NEW quote provides more detail (reason for closure, day of the week) but the core fact (closure) is the same. The NEW quote refers to 'Monday' and the EXISTING quote refers to September 6, 2026, which was a Sunday, however, looking at the 'as_of' dates: NEW is 2026-09-07 (Monday) and EXISTING is 2026-09-06 (Sunday). Wait, if NEW says 'closed on Monday' and EXISTING says 'did not open' as of Sep 6, they might be different days. Let's re-evaluate. September 6, 2026 is a Sunday. Monday is September 7. The NEW quote says 'closed on Monday'. The EXISTING quote 'did not open' is anchored to Sep 6. These are likely different days of closure or the strike continued. However, they both describe the same event (the closure/strike). I will mark as equivalent as they describe the same state of the tower being closed during the protest.",
